% A temporary defined twice in one block, the second time from itself,
% for the validator's gate (rocq/scripts/valid.sh; docs/rocq.md). A definition
% dominates a use in its own block only when it comes strictly before
% it (site_dominates/4's I0 < I). The mutant that deletes the first
% definition leaves `let(tmp(a), w, add, [tmp(a), tmp(k)])` using the
% result it defines: valid_module/1 rejects it, and so must the model;
% one that compared the indices with =< would accept it. The harness
% judges valid modules only, so the module is valid as written and the
% mutant is what tests the boundary: the full campaign
% (nanofil-rocq-full) runs it, the routine smoke check does not. There
% are no run lines. The allocation makes it a Fil-C module.
func(self_use, export, w, [param(w, tmp(k))], [
    block(b0, [], [
        let(tmp(m), p, alloc(8), [const(8)]),
        let(tmp(a), w, add, [tmp(k), const(1)]),
        let(tmp(a), w, add, [tmp(a), tmp(k)])
    ], ret(tmp(a)))
]).
